er/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(h(y))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309192} {:answer/id #uuid "78557d30-e001-5f5a-a26b-4ffee8f45587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309693} {:answer/id #uuid "aed47137-cd74-5a3a-8e1a-468e1c639da8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310161} {:answer/id #uuid "e90e70bf-1af1-5f04-905d-01db63774a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-h(y))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310599}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309693} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f2549b8-3209-5ee0-911e-85760f890fc7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "264d7e3d-1024-501a-b6b9-8a55c0283ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309033} {:answer/id #uuid "6bbb00f5-c95d-5619-9711-1466fb9b2256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309585} {:answer/id #uuid "f0c44eb3-f18a-5f1c-a879-f76fe8a5a3bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310666} {:answer/id #uuid "f1e378b3-fd34-56ee-b56a-fced6df19280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310675}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309585} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3538ac0-16e0-5e97-a1d5-ee3c468b3453" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311267} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9bbe708-fe92-510b-8d49-4004ae8084d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310365} {:answer/id #uuid "dd050e27-f625-5343-b889-6bcde3f1e5d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310520} {:answer/id #uuid "edce2afb-b396-55ec-803b-19aa7fc618a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-({y}^{3}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310640} {:answer/id #uuid "f5501100-5f69-5621-bccf-877b8a6db1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310699}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310699} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc26f1a9-2294-5423-a66b-889e19f78e81" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45f662e8-542b-5be9-816b-1defdf22619f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309284} {:answer/id #uuid "64ad37e6-739d-5ef7-96c6-1a6c1d98b828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309523} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6aa404-eaf3-550e-93a2-45e9996142df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310274} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8908fc-0913-50d5-9ce4-15acfd6cdd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310515}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309284} :answer-field/id #uuid "f10a106b-ae20-5011-a556-104dc38d854a" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e724372-1748-58b7-9601-c50906401bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({y}^{3}+1)(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308978} {:answer/id #uuid "86003a6c-5193-5af9-9edc-5d9430b865b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309794} {:answer/id #uuid "98af1f00-b7e2-5276-97e7-b34eb2cd80fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-3y}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309978} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f51c5f-4184-57b1-a82a-cd4444a19cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-({y}^{3}+1)}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310219}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309794} :answer-field/id #uuid "f41b1634-09e9-5ef2-884f-41911521ab81" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dbfd1646-4161-5287-89b4-1be0e0c83510" :question/math-academy-id "q-337707" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}{y}^{'}=-x{y}^{3}-x,\\hspace{1em}x>0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form. This gives\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=x({y}^{3}+1),\\hspace{2em}Q(x,y)={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\hspace{0.278em}{{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\hspace{0.278em}{{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $y$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-7}},\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form: \n\n$$\nx({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=x({y}^{3}+1),\\,Q(x,y)={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x({y}^{3}+1))=3x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{x({y}^{3}+1)}(3x{y}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $y$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{3}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(y)\\cdot (x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=I(y)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e617450-43e8-5abe-b711-55c66f7eedaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{t}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308846} {:answer/id #uuid "1e242e11-fc07-5c22-ba05-9be291d6372f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{t}^{2}-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308976} {:answer/id #uuid "7a739002-c8a3-5f62-8e33-a3e161ee65d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{t}^{2}-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309701} {:answer/id #uuid "8df8861d-53ee-51cb-b585-59e91d5a65fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309877} {:answer/id #uuid "c8bf282c-c85d-5b89-90a8-45f21c8457f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{t}^{2}+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310358} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3109ada-d6b9-5a56-b743-64fc5cb5f0b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c5583cd7-45bf-57f0-9c2b-4cb14407a01b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337713" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+3\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right).\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then the general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\left(\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}\\right)f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{3}{t(1-t)}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{3}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2/(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t-1|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(t-1)^{2}\\frac{2x}{t-1} & =(t-1)^{2}\\frac{3}{t(1-t)} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =\\frac{3(1-t)}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{3(1-t)}{t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{3(1-t)}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\int (\\frac{3}{t}-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C \\\\ x & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}+3t,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\left(\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}\\right){t}^{2}+3t.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)={t}^{2},\\,g(t)=3t,$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)={t}^{2}+3t.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b93f245-065a-5185-93d4-362871323a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{t}^{2}-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309436} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf62c93-3c68-5005-a0a5-44ce1102a4cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{t}^{2}-t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309860} {:answer/id #uuid "9feccca2-418c-54e0-b9e3-670e953d7f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310040} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a54200-1ebf-508f-8cc9-818acba425db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{t}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310200} {:answer/id #uuid "ca259ff8-ab57-573c-8822-ba8b0ebe9797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{t}^{2}+2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310368}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309436} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b337c6e-8a90-5309-a7b0-a728b817c334" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1184c7b6-6662-5793-8da6-caaadcf27409" :question/math-academy-id "q-337721" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}-2\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right).\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\left(\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-6t+{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}}\\right)f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{2-t}{t(1-t)}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{2-t}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2/(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t-1|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =(t-1)^{2}\\frac{2-t}{t(1-t)} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =\\frac{(1-t)(2-t)}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{2-t}{t}(1-t) \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{2-t}{t}(1-t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\int (\\frac{2}{t}-3+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-6t+{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-6t+{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}-2t,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =\\left(\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-6t+{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}}\\right){t}^{2}-2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)={t}^{2},\\text{ }g(t)=-2t,$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)={t}^{2}-2t.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0453cd41-d901-5009-8f65-b4cfa22bbf3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{t}^{2}+t-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308776} {:answer/id #uuid "968fb4e3-ef61-5e36-9a5e-745bf0584f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{t}^{2}-t-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309955} {:answer/id #uuid "b7ac9c38-fc14-5221-bccf-d2099caf9760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{t}^{2}+t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310234} {:answer/id #uuid "cb999aec-912d-5ca1-8862-8e6e0ddbe6d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{t}^{2}-t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310379} {:answer/id #uuid "f9fff5b2-a814-58fe-916f-2b7cf8737f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{t}^{2}+t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310740}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310740} :answer-field/id #uuid "65612883-612c-5a33-92a8-cd25d69a5a58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "06aec42c-90c8-5e5c-a056-f5d209f3a8f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-337727" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2)-{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=(C{e}^{-t/2}+2t-4)f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{2}x=t.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t/2}\\,\\text{d}t=(2t-4){e}^{t/2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{2}x=t.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{t/2} & =t{e}^{t/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t/2}) & =t{e}^{t/2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t/2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int t{e}^{t/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t/2} & =(2t-4){e}^{t/2}+C \\\\ x & =2t-4+C{e}^{-t/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t/2}+2t-4.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x(t+2)-{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =(C{e}^{-t/2}+2t-4)(t+2)-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)=t+2,\\text{ }g(t)=-{t}^{2},$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)=-{t}^{2}+t+2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ae1e0e-3214-5887-a729-309c961fbd75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "nonlinear" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310120} {:answer/id #uuid "b93668a2-9df7-55ae-9946-dfcbafb7cde5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "linear" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310120} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e5496f6-3e7a-5617-973a-4c86197e42f4" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310874} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64892727-99b0-560e-98f0-30da810430ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "L(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aL({y}_{1})+bL({y}_{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309521} {:answer/id #uuid "6c79d0a6-f429-5985-8082-c52185e0bdad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "L(a{y}_{1}\\cdot b{y}_{2})=abL({y}_{1})\\cdot L({y}_{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309589} {:answer/id #uuid "912fd9cc-7377-523d-b9f4-719d2670816d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\ne aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309909} {:answer/id #uuid "d65d0e3c-0134-5e31-9668-385646533e88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "L(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=L({y}_{1})+L({y}_{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310476}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309909} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c55f04b-e8bc-5e62-a4af-43337733cde0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310953} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46d0acf6-d8e3-5503-9d8a-ecad4067e55a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+b{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309289} {:answer/id #uuid "76bdbccd-516a-5db6-9025-9ee34116846f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{a}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}-{b}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309675} {:answer/id #uuid "90a28d8d-fe61-5189-976f-b72e75148997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{a}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309901}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309901} :answer-field/id #uuid "c09128e8-e1f3-5f9d-bce1-f0d8e0788eee" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311347} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5acefa0e-75be-5722-b86f-46337e5caafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309429} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1c23c9-63ec-537f-b466-5814158b88c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310124} {:answer/id #uuid "bbcbcdde-f0e2-5ef5-affd-1725802db5bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "nonlinear" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310270}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310270} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1e0f51b-ff68-52f7-860e-60fabba672f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ab8c163-345d-5a90-bd2b-86e83c7b97c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309428} {:answer/id #uuid "5eff945b-a812-5204-a190-a6a1a60f493f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\ne aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309459}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309459} :answer-field/id #uuid "f729c200-f282-504c-99fd-9d268dc75252" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3ac9026-19ae-5eaf-8ff6-93a84d074a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310454} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e4b69d-588d-5019-b0be-bb3b68ae279c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310669}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310669} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9843f0-4669-56d8-8d49-34df0a324594" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8be7f3a8-564a-541b-b0e3-87934741ee59" :question/math-academy-id "q-337728" :question/problem "Consider the following differential operator:\n\n$$\nD(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}\n$$\n\nFill in the steps in the reasoning below.\n\nFor any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={{field-2}}+{{field-3}} \\\\  & +2ab\\cdot {{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+b{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since {{field-5}} \nthe operator $D$ is {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "For any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aL({y}_{1})+bL({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+{(\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}))}^{2} \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{(a\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2} \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+2ab\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & +2ab\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is *not* the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}]+b[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}] \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+b{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\ne aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}),$ the operator $D$ is $\\text{nonlinear}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90f63096-9e44-5d1c-8dc8-5b733c7f2352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309907} {:answer/id #uuid "fb38179b-17f5-5e87-aa65-841f87032430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\ne aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310752}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310752} :answer-field/id #uuid "15f8abd5-803c-516f-89fa-ade5aed73367" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fd63877-7c7a-5fe9-